# ============================================================
#  ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES — TEMPLATE
# ============================================================
#  This project is a fully static site. It ships with NO required
#  environment variables and contains NO secrets, API keys or
#  credentials of any kind.
#
#  The contact form runs in demo mode by default (see
#  `formConfig.endpoint` in src/data/portfolio.js): submissions are
#  simulated locally and nothing is sent anywhere.
#
#  This file exists only so that .env is already ignored and so that
#  adding a real endpoint later is obvious. Copy it only if needed:
#
#      cp .env.example .env
#
#  NEVER commit a real .env file — it is ignored by .gitignore.
#  ------------------------------------------------------------


# Optional — public contact-form endpoint (Formspree, Formspark,
# your own API route, ...). Leave empty to keep demo mode.
# VITE_CONTACT_ENDPOINT=


# Note for maintainers:
#   * Only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the client
#     bundle by Vite, and they are therefore PUBLIC — never put a
#     secret, private API key or password in a VITE_* variable.
#   * Any secret a backend needs must stay on that backend and must
#     never be shipped to the browser.
#   * No variable below is referenced by the code today; add the
#     import in src/data/portfolio.js at the same time you set one.